    {
      "id": "node-composition-section-2",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Root contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": -640
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Root contract",
        "body": "A new graph starts with one root and its identity and intent payloads:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"root\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"graphId\": \"example-graph\",\n      \"name\": \"Example Graph\",\n      \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n      \"description\": \"A small graph.\"\n    },\n    \"intent\": { \"kind\": \"graph\", \"scope\": \"local\" },\n    \"root\": { \"kind\": \"graph\", \"defaultSurfaceId\": \"default\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe root is the implicit root Port. Do not create a second root Port node. Author one `surface` edge for each Surface, an optional `ground` edge for the inside frame, and `exposes-port` edges only when additional named interfaces are needed.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "node-composition"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
