    {
      "id": "node-composition-section-3",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Surface and face contract",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Surface and face contract",
        "body": "A Surface is an ordered chain:\n\n1. a `surface` edge leaves the root and targets the first `face`;\n2. each additional face follows through a `next-face` edge from `sequence-out` to `sequence-in`;\n3. the final face points to a `glyph` through the same chain relationship.\n\nOne face is enough. Add another only when it conveys a useful smaller representation. Do not manufacture Detail, Summary, and Icon faces merely to fill named bands. The resolver uses the nearest authored face as the workspace becomes smaller.\n\nThe root-to-ground geometry defines the authored interface frame when a graph has ground. Size that frame to include material that must remain visible in unfocused rendering and the Minimap representation. The active graph's main minimap covers the complete graph and is a navigation instrument.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "node-composition"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
